There are several ways you can implement this method.  This is one way to do it.



Initialize Variables:

Create an instance of Scanner using System.in to read input from the user.

Initialize variables sum and count to keep track of the sum and the number of entered integers.

Initialize avg as a long to store the average.

Loop for Input:

Use a while loop that runs indefinitely (while (true)) to continuously read input.

Inside the loop:

Check if the scanner has the next integer using scanner.hasNextInt().

If there's an integer, add it to the sum, increment the count, and consume the line separator with scanner.nextLine() to move to the next line.

If the input is not an integer, break out of the loop to stop reading input.

Calculate Average:

After the loop, check if count is greater than 0.

If count is greater than 0, calculate the average by dividing sum by count and round it to the nearest integer using Math.round().

Print Result:

Print the calculated sum and avg using System.out.println() with appropriate messages.

Close Scanner:

Close the Scanner using scanner.close() to release the resources associated with it.

